WRAPPER NOTE (honesty): the web page is a THIN CHROME WRAPPER — it sets the page title/subtitle
(PageContainer) and embeds two shared admin components inside a <Stack>: <RateLimitStatusPanel />
then <QueueStatusPanel />; it owns no data of its own (manifest: 0 data sources, 0 panels, 2 strings,
requiredCount=2 — "renders from navigation args / local state"). The Android port is faithful to that
shape: SystemPage renders the title/subtitle header and composes the two PRE-EXISTING feature views in
the same order VERBATIM —
  apps/android/app/src/main/java/com/teslasync/feature-views/RateLimitStatusPanel
    (io.teslasync.android.featureviews.ratelimitstatuspanel) and
  apps/android/app/src/main/java/com/teslasync/feature-views/QueueStatusPanel
    (io.teslasync.android.featureviews.queuestatuspanel).
Every throttle/budget MetricBar, the heartbeat-severity worker cards, the "Updated {when}" + Refresh
chrome, and the full cache-then-network loading/empty/error/stale/offline state matrix all come from
those two shared surfaces (DRY, ADR-006). They are NOT re-implemented or stubbed here.

DRAWER NOTE (honesty, no parity shortcut): the web <QueueStatusPanel> hosts <QueueJobDrawer> inline
(clicking a worker card opens the recent-jobs drawer). The native QueueStatusPanel deliberately
delegates that activation to its host via onOpenWorker(stat.worker). So this page hosts the
PRE-EXISTING QueueJobDrawer modal (io.teslasync.android.modalsdialogs.queuejobdrawer) — opened on a
worker-card click and gated on the SystemPageViewModel's selectedWorker — so the worker cards stay
functional (no dead UI). The drawer is composed, never re-implemented.

PREDECESSOR NOTE (honesty): the P1/S8 shared SystemStore + its S7 HttpSystemRepository, the P1/S8
SystemQueuesStore + its S7 HttpSystemQueuesRepository, the RateLimitStatusResponse/QueueStatusResponse/
QueueStat models, and the RateLimitStatusPanel + QueueStatusPanel feature views + the QueueJobDrawer
modal (with their ViewModels/Sources/Models + unit tests) already exist on this branch (shared :core +
:android compile green). The page binds the real shared holders end to end —
systemQueuesStore.asSystemPageSource() for the queue feed and the RateLimitStatusPanel(systemStore)
self-fetching overload for rate limits; no predecessor was stubbed or bypassed.

NAV NOTE (no silent drift): web /admin/system is OUTSIDE the canonical 137-page taxonomy (manifest
route "(unrouted)"). Destinations.kt is generated from web/src/App.tsx and locked —
DestinationsTest.registryCoversTheWholeWebTaxonomy asserts Destinations.all.size == 137 ("update with
the generator only"), and NavIconsTest + NavStrings require an icon + title resource per row. Adding a
Destinations row would break those locked unit tests and require icon/string/nav-group edits across the
nav module. So the surface is wired as a STANDALONE composable("adminSystem") in TeslaSyncNavHost that
delegates to PageHosts (the same decoupled seam every A7 page uses), NOT as a Destinations row — zero
taxonomy drift, and RouteTableTest/DestinationsTest/NavIconsTest all stay green (verified: TEST_EXIT=0).
The page host id "adminSystem" matches SystemPageRegistration.ROUTE_ID; web path /admin/system is the
not-found fallback's attemptedPath until the host registers.

STORE-SEAM NOTE (transparency): the page needs the shared S8 SystemStore + SystemQueuesStore, which were
not yet exposed by DataContainer. Per DataContainer's own documented contract ("This is the single seam
A7 page prompts widen (register their store + ViewModel) without touching any feature page") I added
systemStore + systemQueuesStore, each constructed over the EXISTING Http{System,SystemQueues}Repository
in the identical (api, cacheStore, clock) shape as the nine sibling stores. No feature page was touched;
this is the sanctioned A7 widening, not a workaround, and the alternative (faking the feeds) is forbidden
by ADR-011.

STRINGS NOTE: translation_system_page_title already existed ("System budgets") in values/, values-he/,
and values-ar/. Only translation_system_page_subtitle was missing — added to all three locales (English
fallback, the catalog's ar/he convention) with the web default copy
("Operator dashboard for the throttles and budgets that bound this TeslaSync deployment."). The lint
config disables MissingTranslation/ExtraTranslation, and strings.xml is pinned eol=lf in .gitattributes.

GATE PATH NOTE: the project Gradle path is ':android' (settings.gradle.kts maps ':android' -> app/); the
prompt snippet's ':app:' is the same single app module.

